# Milestone 27: uppercase, letter spacing and small caps (reference/common/typography.md). Page of 200 × 200 with
# margins of 20: page area of 160 × 160 from (20, 20). Lines of 12 (Size 10); with the test metrics
# each character measures 5 pt. Language es: Case follows the rules of Spanish.
#   row:     Stack at (20, 20), 160 × 12; its items take their natural width and follow one another:
#     spaced   "abcd" with Letter spacing 2: 4 × 5 + 3 × 2 (the last one does not carry it) = 26. x = 20.
#     small    "Ab" with Small caps: the A measures 5 and the b, turned into B, 80 % of 5 = 4: 9. x = 46.
#     upper    "straße" with Case uppercase: STRASSE is 7 characters: 35. x = 55.
#     plain    "abcd" with nothing: 20. x = 90.
#   tight:   29 characters, 145 pt: it fits in the line of 160: 12. y = 32.
#   loose:   the same text with Letter spacing 2: each character advances 7 and the width is 7n − 2 ≤ 160,
#            n ≤ 23; the first line is "aaaa bbbb cccc dddd" (19; with " eeee" it would be 24) and the
#            second "eeee ffff": 24. y = 44.
#   title:   Case uppercase and Letter spacing 3 do not change the height: 12. y = 68.
#   caps:    Small caps with Letter spacing 1, one line: 12. y = 80.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 200
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
	Section:
		Stack:
			Id: row
			Item:
				Text: abcd
					Id: spaced
					Typography:
						Letter spacing: 2
			Item:
				Text: Ab
					Id: small
					Typography:
						Small caps: true
			Item:
				Text: straße
					Id: upper
					Typography:
						Case: uppercase
			Item:
				Text: abcd
					Id: plain
		Text: aaaa bbbb cccc dddd eeee ffff
			Id: tight
		Text: aaaa bbbb cccc dddd eeee ffff
			Id: loose
			Typography:
				Letter spacing: 2
		Text: informe anual
			Id: title
			Typography:
				Case: uppercase
				Letter spacing: 3
		Text: Pequeñas Mayúsculas
			Id: caps
			Typography:
				Small caps: true
				Letter spacing: 1
